index 000000000..db3b73ad7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/whatsnew/fragments/7229.bugfix
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+Commas that are part of a regular expression (escaped as ``\,``, or inside a
+quantifier like ``{1,3}``, a group or a character class) are no longer treated as
+separators in options taking a comma-separated list of regular expressions,
+such as ``bad-names-rgxs``.
+
+Closes #7229
